<DocsLayout
  title="Effects"
  description="Post-processing filters applied to a scene's output."
>
  <p>
    Effects process the rendered output of their parent scene. They stack in
    order &mdash; the top of the Effects list runs first. Like displays, they
    can be reordered, toggled, and bound to reactors.
  </p>

  <h2>Adding an effect</h2>
  <p>
    Click the <strong>+</strong> in the Effects row of a scene and pick from the
    menu. Effects are grouped by category.
  </p>
  <div class="placeholder">Screenshot: Add Effects menu open</div>

  <h2>Color</h2>
  <ul class="pill-list">
    <li>Color</li>
    <li>Brightness / Contrast</li>
    <li>Hue / Saturation</li>
    <li>Sepia</li>
    <li>Tone Mapping</li>
    <li>Color Average</li>
    <li>Color Depth</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Tone and color grading. Color tints the whole scene with a blend mode.</p>

  <h2>Blur &amp; Focus</h2>
  <ul class="pill-list">
    <li>Blur</li>
    <li>Bloom</li>
    <li>Depth of Field</li>
    <li>Tilt Shift</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Soften parts of the image or add a cinematic glow.</p>

  <h2>Distortion</h2>
  <ul class="pill-list">
    <li>Distortion</li>
    <li>Glitch</li>
    <li>Kaleidoscope</li>
    <li>Mirror</li>
    <li>RGB Shift</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Warp, displace, or chromatically split the image.</p>

  <h2>Pattern</h2>
  <ul class="pill-list">
    <li>ASCII</li>
    <li>Color Halftone</li>
    <li>Dot Screen</li>
    <li>LED</li>
    <li>Pixelate</li>
    <li>Scanline</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Overlay a repeating pattern that turns the scene into dots, pixels, or characters.</p>

  <h2>Stylize</h2>
  <ul class="pill-list">
    <li>Noise</li>
    <li>Perlin Noise</li>
    <li>Vignette</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Film-grain, procedural noise, and edge falloff.</p>

  <h2>Ordering matters</h2>
  <p>
    Effect order changes the final look. Bloom before Color produces a different
    result than Color before Bloom. Drag to reorder in the Layers panel.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
